Some patches modify the bundled or dependent libraries rather than the system itself: MOAI-CPU's
patches touch the bundled SEAL (for example systems/moai-cpu/impl/patch_poolcensus.py), MOAI-GPU's
touch the bundled Phantom library (for example systems/moai-gpu/impl/pin_seed_and_gate.py and
patch_modraise.py), and ARION's a1 lever reimplements Lattigo's bootstrapping ShallowCopy
(systems/arion/impl/patch_shallowcopy.py). Those changes are under the license of the library they
modify: MIT for SEAL, GPL-3.0 for Phantom, Apache-2.0 for Lattigo.

MOAI (github.com/dtc2025ag/MOAI), MOAI_GPU (github.com/dtc2025ag/MOAI_GPU) and Arion
(github.com/hangenba/Arion) carry no license upstream: their repositories have no license file
(checked 2026-09-29). For these three this repository contains only changes to their code (patch
scripts under systems/moai-cpu/, systems/moai-gpu/ and systems/arion/, which rewrite named upstream
files at build time) and references to the pinned upstream commits; it contains no complete
upstream source file of any of them. The closest to one are three header fragments in
systems/moai-gpu/impl/borrowed/ that the MOAI-GPU patches insert into the upstream tree:
layernorm1_streaming.cuh and layernorm2_streaming.cuh are streaming rewrites of MOAI_GPU's
layernorm functions (source/non_linear_func/layernorm.cuh), and wpark_helpers.cuh holds
campaign-written helpers. Nothing in this repository grants any license to MOAI, MOAI_GPU or Arion
code, and the MIT License in LICENSE does not extend to it. The changes are published to make the
measurements reproducible; any reuse of the upstream code needs its authors' permission.

The Apache License 2.0 requires modified files to carry notices that they were changed. The
patches for BumbleBee, PUMA and ARION's Lattigo change identify the upstream files they change, in
the diff headers or as the file path each patch script rewrites.
